  "title": "Options are tools for trade-offs, not magic strategies",
  "summary": "There is no magic option strategy. Options are tools that reshape the distribution of a stock's returns. Every choice is a trade-off: current income costs you upside, and convexity costs you premium. Judge each trade by its asymmetry and its probability.",
